A destroy that spares the pools below
leaves them naming a parent that is gone.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-grain32 fuzz-work test qemu-replay
Report: pool's parent is not a live, older pool

diff --git a/kernel/pool.c b/kernel/pool.c
--- a/kernel/pool.c
+++ b/kernel/pool.c
@@ -61,3 +61,3 @@ void pool_destroy(struct pool *pool)
         next = pool_next_pool(p);
-        if (!pool_under(p, pool)) {
+        if (p != pool) {
             kept = p;
